## Features I'd genuinely add (beyond what I mentioned before), and why each earns its place

- **Undo toast** — every destructive/state-changing action (mark complete, delete note, clear revision flag) gets a 5-second "Undone" toast with an undo button. Costs little, removes a huge class of "oh no I misclicked" anxiety in a tool used for months.
- **Keyboard shortcuts on desktop** — `/` to search, `j/k` to move through topic list, `space` to toggle complete. Power users studying at a desk for hours will genuinely use this.
- **Session-based time tracking (optional, local-only)** — a simple start/stop timer per subject, stored locally, feeding the "pace" estimate with real hours instead of just topic counts. Not forced — a student who doesn't want to track time never sees it get in the way.
- **Local reminders via the Notification API** — "You haven't touched Polity in 9 days" — opt-in, no backend needed, works fine as a static PWA.
- **Print/export a clean revision sheet** — one click to a printable page of just pending + flagged topics, for offline last-week cramming when data/battery is unreliable — genuinely how a lot of exam prep happens in the final days.
- **Data export/import as JSON** — already agreed, but I'd make it prominent (in Home settings, not buried), since guest/localStorage users have literally no backup otherwise and losing months of tracked progress is a real, high-stakes failure mode for this app specifically.
- **Conflict-safe sync indicator** — a small, honest "synced" / "saving…" / "offline — will sync" indicator near the profile icon, so students on patchy hostel wifi aren't left wondering if their progress is actually saved. Trust in the data is the whole product.

## What I'd deliberately not build

- No badges/points/leaderboards — exam prep stress doesn't need gamified competition layered on top.
- No social/sharing features — adds backend complexity this static-site + Firebase architecture isn't suited for, and isn't why students use this.
- No AI-generated study plans or chatbot — out of scope, adds fragility and cost for a tool whose value is being simple and fast.
- No forced daily streak guilt-tripping — streak is shown, never punished.

