## Visual & interaction system, more specifically

- Distinct exam-accent colors, but used **sparingly** — as thin left-borders and small icons, not full card backgrounds, so the UI doesn't look like a color-coded mess when all three exams are visible at once.
- Motion used only for state confirmation (a checkbox settling, a card collapsing) — never decorative animation that delays getting to content.
- One real "moment" reserved for completing an entire subject (100%) — a brief, tasteful animation — because that's a genuine milestone worth marking, versus overusing celebration on every small tick.
- Typography carries most of the visual identity: a confident large numeral style for stats, restrained body text elsewhere — letting content density read as "serious study tool," not "consumer app."

